      "s load balancing",
      "s load balancers",
      "global external application load balancers can use service load balancing policies to control backend traffic distribution parameters such as algorithm choice and auto capacity draining",
      "classic application load balancer resources can be migrated to the global external application load balancer infrastructure by changing the load balancing scheme to external managed",
      "cloud load balancing supports failover for global classic and regional external application load balancers by using regional external application load balancers as backups",
      "internal passthrough network load balancers can load balance multiple layer 3 and layer 4 protocols including tcp udp icmp icmpv6 sctp esp ah and gre",
      "internal and external application load balancers support cleartext http 2 over tcp including backend connections configured with the h2c protocol",
      "global and regional external application load balancers can mirror only a configured percentage of requests to a mirrored backend service",
      "global external application load balancers can designate preferred backends to optimize traffic placement for cost latency and resiliency",
      "global external application load balancers support backend certificate validation and mutual tls for load balancer to backend connections",
      "application load balancers can distribute traffic based on user defined custom metrics instead of standard utilization or rate metrics",
      "network endpoint groups support global internet endpoints so cloud cdn can use custom origins hosted on premises or in other clouds",
      "internal and external passthrough network load balancers support connection draining for udp and other non tcp protocol traffic",
      "the cloud load balancing console can display the equivalent api resources for load balancer create and update actions",
      "internal tcp udp load balancing supports distributing traffic across multiple nics on a single backend vm instance",
      "iam conditions supports forwarding rule attributes to control which types of forwarding rules a member can create",
      "cross region internal application load balancers can route requests for static content to cloud storage buckets",
      "application load balancers support authorization policies to enforce access control checks on incoming traffic",
